The 2020–21 '''Saudi Pro League''' was the 46th edition of the [[Saudi Pro League|top-tier Saudi football league]], established in [[1974–75 Saudi Categorization League|1974]], and the 13th edition since it was rebranded as the '''Saudi Pro League''' in [[2008–09 Saudi Pro League|2008]], the season began on 17 October 2020 as a consequence of the postponement of the previous season's conclusion due to the [[COVID-19 pandemic]].<ref>{{cite web |title=الدوري السعودي ينتهي في 9 سبتمبر.. والنسخة الجديدة تنطلق منتصف أكتوبر |url=https://www.alarabiya.net/ar/sport/saudi-sport/2020/06/18/%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AF%D9%88%D8%B1%D9%8A-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B3%D8%B9%D9%88%D8%AF%D9%8A-%D9%8A%D9%86%D8%AA%D9%87%D9%8A-%D9%81%D9%8A-9-%D8%B3%D8%A8%D8%AA%D9%85%D8%A8%D8%B1-%D9%88%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%86%D8%B3%D8%AE%D8%A9-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AC%D8%AF%D9%8A%D8%AF%D8%A9-%D8%AA%D9%86%D8%B7%D9%84%D9%82-%D9%85%D9%86%D8%AA%D8%B5%D9%81-%D8%A3%D9%83%D8%AA%D9%88%D8%A8%D8%B1}}</ref> Fixtures for the 2020–21 season were announced on 29 September 2020.<ref>{{cite web |title=رسميا.. جدول الدور الأول من الدوري السعودي 2020-2021 | date=29 September 2020 |url=https://www.kooora.com/?n=959924}}</ref>

==Overview==
[[Al Hilal SFC|Al-Hilal]] are the defending champions after winning the Pro League for the 16th time last season.<ref>{{cite web |title=قبل النهاية بجولتَيْن.. الهلال يُتوَّج بلقب دوري كأس الأمير محمد بن سلمان |date=29 August 2020 |url=https://sabq.org/6MCPYD}}</ref> [[Al-Ain FC (Saudi Arabia)|Al-Ain]], [[Al-Batin FC|Al-Batin]], and [[Al-Qadsiah FC|Al-Qadsiah]] join as the three promoted clubs from the [[2019–20 Prince Mohammad bin Salman League|2019–20 MS League]].<ref>{{cite web |title=القادسية يلحق بالعين والباطن.. إلى دوري المحترفين |date=10 September 2020 |url=https://sabq.org/Y3MGzn}}</ref> They replace [[Al-Adalah FC|Al-Adalah]], [[Al-Fayha FC|Al-Fayha]], and [[Al-Hazem F.C.|Al-Hazem]] who were relegated to the [[2020–21 Prince Mohammad bin Salman League|2020–21 MS League]].

On 29 March, the [[Ministry of Sports of Saudi Arabia|Ministry of Sports]] announced that fans will be allowed to return to stadiums for the final three rounds of matches with a maximum of 40% capacity.<ref>{{cite web |title=عودة الجماهير لملاعب السعودية.. بشرط! |url=https://www.alarabiya.net/saudi-today/2021/03/29/%D8%B9%D9%88%D8%AF%D8%A9-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AC%D9%85%D8%A7%D9%87%D9%8A%D8%B1-%D9%84%D9%85%D9%84%D8%A7%D8%B9%D8%A8-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B3%D8%B9%D9%88%D8%AF%D9%8A%D8%A9-%D8%A8%D9%86%D8%B3%D8%A8%D8%A9-40-%D8%A8%D8%B4%D8%B1%D8%B7}}</ref> 

On 23 May, [[Al Hilal SFC|Al-Hilal]] secured their seventeenth league title with one match to spare following a 1–0 away win against [[Al-Taawoun FC|Al-Taawoun]]. It was also the club's second consecutive title and fourth in the last five seasons.<ref>{{cite web |title=فريق الهلال يُحقق لقب دوري الأمير محمد بن سلمان للمحترفين قبل جولة من ختام من المسابقة |url=https://www.spa.gov.sa/viewfullstory.php?lang=ar&newsid=2230529}}</ref> [[Al-Ain FC (Saudi Arabia)|Al-Ain]] were the first team to be relegated following a 2–0 defeat away to [[Al-Nassr FC|Al-Nassr]] on 14 May.<ref>{{cite web |title=رسميا.. العين اول الهابطين من الدوري السعودي للمحترفين |url=https://alwafd.news/%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B1%D9%8A%D8%A7%D8%B6%D8%A9/3742665-%D8%B1%D8%B3%D9%85%D9%8A%D8%A7-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B9%D9%8A%D9%86-%D8%A7%D9%88%D9%84-%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%87%D8%A7%D8%A8%D8%B7%D9%8A%D9%86-%D9%85%D9%86-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AF%D9%88%D8%B1%D9%8A-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B3%D8%B9%D9%88%D8%AF%D9%8A-%D9%84%D9%84%D9%85%D8%AD%D8%AA%D8%B1%D9%81%D9%8A%D9%86}}</ref> In the final matchday, both [[Al-Qadsiah FC|Al-Qadsiah]] and [[Al-Wehda Club (Mecca)|Al-Wehda]] were relegated following a draw with [[Abha Club|Abha]] and a loss against [[Al-Shabab FC (Riyadh)|Al-Shabab]] respectively.<ref>{{cite web |title=الوحدة والقادسية يودعان.. وضمك والباطن وأبها ينجون |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/731383}}</ref>

