Sixteen teams will compete in the league&nbsp;– the top thirteen teams from the previous season and the three teams promoted from the [[2019–20 Prince Mohammad bin Salman League|MS League]].

'''Teams who were promoted to the Pro League'''

The first club to be promoted was [[Al-Batin FC|Al-Batin]], who were promoted following [[Al-Bukayriyah FC|Al-Bukayriyah's]] 1–1 draw with [[Al-Ain FC (Saudi Arabia)|Al-Ain]] on 1 September 2020. Al-Batin will play in the top flight of Saudi football after a season's absence.<ref>{{cite web |title=عاد للأضواء للمرة الرابعة.. الباطن أول المتأهلين لدوري المحترفين |date=September 2020 |url=https://sabq.org/Rc52Kt}}</ref> Al-Batin were crowned champions following their 1–1 draw with Al-Bukayriyah on the final matchday.<ref>{{cite web |title=الباطن.. بطلا بـ76 نقطة |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/702635}}</ref>

The second club to be promoted was [[Al-Ain FC (Saudi Arabia)|Al-Ain]], who were promoted on 10 September 2020 following their 2–0 win at home against [[Ohod Club|Ohod]].<ref>{{cite web |title=بعد 44 عاما.. العين يعانق الأضواء |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/701530}}</ref> Al-Ain will play in the top flight of Saudi football for the first time in history. Al-Ain became the first team from the [[Al Bahah Region]] to play in the Pro League.

The third and final club to be promoted was [[Al-Qadsiah FC|Al-Qadsiah]], following their 3–1 home win against an already promoted Al-Batin side on 10 September 2020.<ref>{{cite web |title=القادسية.. الصعود الخامس |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/701529}}</ref> Al-Qadsiah will play in the top flight of Saudi football after a season's absence.

'''Teams who were relegated to the MS League'''

The first club to be relegated was [[Al-Adalah FC|Al-Adalah]], who were relegated after only a year in the top flight following a 1–1 home draw with [[Al-Raed FC|Al-Raed]].<ref>{{cite web |title=العدالة يهبط رسمياً إلى دوري الدرجة الأولى إثر تعادله مع الرائد |url=http://www.alriyadh.com/1839391}}</ref>

On 4 September 2020, [[Al-Hazem F.C.|Al-Hazem]] became the second club to be relegated following a 1–0 defeat away to [[Al-Shabab FC (Riyadh)|Al-Shabab]].<ref>{{cite web |title=المرة الثانية.. الحزم يهبط |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/700875}}</ref> Al-Hazem were relegated after two years in the top flight.

On 9 September 2020, [[Al-Fayha FC|Al-Fayha]] became the third and final club to be relegated following a 1–0 defeat away to [[Al-Taawoun FC|Al-Taawoun]] in the final matchday.<ref>{{cite web |title=السهلاوي يهزم الكابوس.. ويفجر الأفراح |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/701373}}</ref> Al-Fayha were relegated after three years in the Pro League. This was Al-Fayha's first relegation from the top flight of Saudi football.

